-- title:
--   A carry-indicator box mean is a normalized carry-cell sum
-- statement:
--   For a nonzero modulus $N$, a finite indexed CFZ form family with decidable equality, an integer carry vector, and any real function $F$ on natural-coordinate tuples, the side-$N$ box mean of the carry indicator times $F$ is the sum of $F$ over the canonical carry cell divided by the box volume.
